{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/bo61s4","slideIndex":2,"text":"Both models use home size, rooms, parking, location coordinates, property type, house style, municipality, community, and listing time. The list-aware model also receives list price; the off-market model never sees it. Both models predict log sale price with histogram gradient boosting. The frozen release is the previously published structured-feature version. Remarks predictions remain in a separate experiment archive.\n\nSource: Frozen feature and model definitions: https://github.com/billchenziang33/toronto-home-price-prediction-2026/blob/7cffe186bd9f0a2e8fc22f3897d52b3dbaaa8df8/features.py and https://github.com/billchenziang33/toronto-home-price-prediction-2026/blob/7cffe186bd9f0a2e8fc22f3897d52b3dbaaa8df8/models.py"}
